# mars-schema follow-ups

- Reduce WASM size by replacing duplicate TOML parsing and the YAML structural
  event scan; TOML error text is part of the fixture contract.
- Integer-like mapping keys lose file order across the WASM boundary. Returning
  pairs would preserve it but change the JS contract.
- Installed reads discard upgrade diagnostics. An invalid value combined with a
  pre-v1 spelling can therefore be dropped without warning.
- `frontmatter.too-deep` counts brackets inside quoted strings and can reject
  valid input; count only outside quoted scalars.
